import{_ as n,o as i,c as t,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 356 | Perfect-Work Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Realm Inflation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 356 | Perfect-Work Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Realm Inflation","no":356,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Perfect World","Law-First Axiom","Realm Inflation","Comparison","Retcon"],"related":["14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification","11-Deduction Iteration System Detail","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0356_模块2-完美世界-衡元宙如何避免境界膨胀.md","filePath":"en/0356_模块2-完美世界-衡元宙如何避免境界膨胀.md"}'),o={name:"en/0356_模块2-完美世界-衡元宙如何避免境界膨胀.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,h,c){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-356-perfect-work-law-first-comparison-how-heng-yuan-zhou-avoids-realm-inflation" tabindex="-1">Entry 356 | Perfect-Work Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Realm Inflation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-356-perfect-work-law-first-comparison-how-heng-yuan-zhou-avoids-realm-inflation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 356 | Perfect-Work Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Realm Inflation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Perfect-Work Full Decomposition (Entry 33 · Comparison) | Benchmark base: Documents 14, 11, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-eighteen-layer-inflation-vs-nine-plus-two-—-the-difference-is-only-the-four-words-law-precedes" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Eighteen-layer inflation vs. nine-plus-two — the difference is only the four words &quot;law precedes&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-eighteen-layer-inflation-vs-nine-plus-two-—-the-difference-is-only-the-four-words-law-precedes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Eighteen-layer inflation vs. nine-plus-two — the difference is only the four words &quot;law precedes&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perfect World&#39;s realms inflate to collapse; Heng Yuan Zhou achieves &quot;infinitely expandable without collapse.&quot; The difference is not in the author&#39;s pen power, but in whether the law-first axiom is adhered to. This entry takes the six top-level axioms as base — anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races, collective ascension axiom, causal self-discipline axiom, law-first axiom (core, this entry&#39;s focus), universal equal infinite law — to compare the two. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Protagonist uniqueness dependency verdict: <strong>Shi Hao = extreme-leaning-medium / single-log tendency</strong>.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-comparison" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Comparison) <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Comparison)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perfect World: to let the protagonist keep leveling, layers added again and again; early iron laws torn up. Heng Yuan Zhou: law precedes; new dimensions joined on appendix terms; early iron laws never shaken.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-comparison" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Comparison) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Comparison)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perfect World: setting gives way to plot; readers no longer trust the rules. Heng Yuan Zhou: setting self-consistency over plot convenience; worldview always credible.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-comparison" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Comparison) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Comparison)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Perfect World: inflated layers = predatory-leveling steps. Heng Yuan Zhou: leveling relies on deduction iteration (one of the Origin Three-Basic), on understanding, not piling resources.</p><h2 id="iv-anchor-symbiosis-alternative-this-entry-s-core-comparison" tabindex="-1">IV. Anchor Symbiosis Alternative (This Entry&#39;s Core Comparison) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-anchor-symbiosis-alternative-this-entry-s-core-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Anchor Symbiosis Alternative (This Entry&#39;s Core Comparison)&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Perfect World (Law Does Not Precede)</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou (Law-First)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Realms</td><td>Eighteen layers, added when plot needs</td><td>Nine-realm skeleton + two-realm appendix, never retcons</td></tr><tr><td>Leveling</td><td>Pile resources</td><td>Deduction-iteration law understanding</td></tr><tr><td>Expansion</td><td>Overturn old setting</td><td>Incremental join</td></tr><tr><td>Reader trust</td><td>Late collapse</td><td>Always credible</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Heng Yuan Zhou Document 11 &quot;Deduction Iteration System&quot; explains: leveling is deepening cognition and deduction, not piling numbers. This is why nine-plus-two can infinitely expand — because what expands is law understanding, not resource numbers.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Replicate the two realm philosophies</li><li>Cross-hundred-thousand-year deduction</li><li>Count setting self-consistency change</li><li>Output &quot;Law-First Comparison Report&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Perfect-Work self-consistency: low; Heng Yuan Zhou: high</strong></li><li><strong>Perfect-Work retcon risk: extreme; Heng Yuan Zhou: zero</strong></li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: extreme-leaning-medium / single-log tendency</strong></li></ul><p>Add one layer: the contest between law-first and plot convenience is essentially who listens to whom. In Perfect World, whoever plot needs to win, whose realm is temporarily sufficient; in Heng Yuan Zhou, law speaks first, plot can only play within law. The former reduces setting to prop; the latter makes setting a contract — whether readers trust a set of rules depends entirely on whether this contract holds.</p><p>One closing line: law is the yoke the author puts on himself; it is precisely this yoke that lets the world survive. Rules never overturned deserve to be called a world.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: no padding, no repeated construction</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: leveling by understanding, not predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo capping at Fierce Realm is already restrained; Heng Yuan Zhou fundamentally eliminates inflation</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: clear steps everyone can walk</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: law-first is precisely designed for infinite expansion</li></ul><p>Add one more layer: law-first&#39;s benefit is giving both author and reader a common contract to rely on. Writing long-form&#39;s greatest fear is not writing too slowly, but writing yourself into collapse. Heng Yuan Zhou uses the nine-realm skeleton to make this collapse institutionally impossible.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-analysis-realm-inflation-prevention-mechanism" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Analysis: Realm-Inflation Prevention Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-analysis-realm-inflation-prevention-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Analysis: Realm-Inflation Prevention Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How does Heng Yuan Zhou avoid realm inflation? The core is the law-first axiom plus the Alaya Network&#39;s consistency check. New realm proposals must pass the network&#39;s logical-compatibility test — it cannot overlap with existing realms&#39; functional positioning, cannot凭空 add layers to manufacture thrills. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s 300 systems are stable architectures long-simulated. The universal equal infinite law ensures realm count does not affect rights equality: whether nine realms or eighteen, everyone&#39;s basic evolution right is unaffected.</p><h2 id="supplementary-analysis-dynamic-assessment-of-realm-count" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Analysis: Dynamic Assessment of Realm Count <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-analysis-dynamic-assessment-of-realm-count" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Analysis: Dynamic Assessment of Realm Count&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s mechanism to avoid realm inflation is the Alaya Network&#39;s dynamic assessment system for realm count. Whenever a new realm is proposed, the network assesses from three dimensions: function overlap with existing realms, logical compatibility with underlying axioms, Myriad-Rank genuine need. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s law-first axiom ensures assessment results cannot be overturned by plot needs. The universal equal infinite law means no matter how many realm layers, everyone&#39;s basic rights unchanged — realms are growth marks, not rights thresholds.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Realm inflation is not the inevitability of &quot;writing long,&quot; but the cost of &quot;law not preceding.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s nine-plus-two proves: as long as law precedes and never retcons, the worldview can be infinitely vast, without using numerical inflation to cover law emptiness.</p><p>In the final analysis, Perfect World · how Heng Yuan Zhou avoids realm inflation described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./329_模块2-完美世界-十八层境界的设定崩坏.html">Entry 329 · Realm Inflation</a> · <a href="./351_模块2-完美世界-九境+二境的稳定框架.html">Entry 351 · Realm-System Alternative</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/14-修炼境界统一划分.html">14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification</a></li></ul>',33)])])}const p=n(o,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
